# Copy this file's variable NAMES into Vercel → your Project → Settings →
# Environment Variables. Never commit a real .env file with real values to
# GitHub — this .env.example file (with no real values) is safe to commit.

# From Razorpay Dashboard → Account & Settings → API Keys ("Key ID").
# This one IS sent to the browser (Razorpay Checkout needs it client-side
# to open the payment popup) — it's a public identifier, not a secret, the
# same idea as a Stripe "publishable key." Returned by /api/create-order.
RAZORPAY_KEY_ID=

# From the same screen ("Key Secret" — only shown once, when generated).
# NEVER put this in index.html or any frontend file. Server-side
# environment variable only, read only by lib/razorpay.js. Used both to
# authenticate API calls and to verify the payment signature Checkout
# hands back to the browser.
RAZORPAY_KEY_SECRET=

# From Razorpay Dashboard → Account & Settings → Webhooks, when you add
# the webhook endpoint. This is NOT auto-generated — you type in your own
# secret when creating the webhook, then copy that exact same value here.
# Used only to verify that webhook calls really came from Razorpay.
RAZORPAY_WEBHOOK_SECRET=

# Added automatically when you attach the "Redis on Vercel" (Upstash)
# storage integration to this project — you will not type these in by
# hand, Vercel fills them in for you. Listed here just so you recognize
# them if you see them in the Vercel dashboard.
# KV_REST_API_URL=
# KV_REST_API_TOKEN=
